    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12946" root="دلص" body-key="d">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدْلَصُ</span></b> ; fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَلْصَآءُ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دِلَاصٌ</span>, near the end of
the paragraph. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Applied to an ass, <i>To which
new hair has grown;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدْلَصِىٌّ</span></b> . (Ibn-
'Abbád, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And the fem., applied to an aged
she-camel, <i>Whose teeth have fallen out</i> (K TA)
<i>by reason of extreme age;</i> (TA;) as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَرْصَآءُ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَلْقَآءُ</span>. (TA.)

